He looked up at the fa\'e7ade of the building which leant ominously over the footpath. Its dusty brickwork and gaunt windows sagged forward to such an extent, the breath of a hearty child might send the whole conglomeration tumbling into the street. Elvi assisted Cracker through the doors. Expensive department store air conditioning smacked them in their faces a like chilled cheesecloth.\
Belying the third-world exterior of the building, the interior had been recently gutted and retrofitted as a very modern, very luxurious recording studio. In back, was an equally opulent two-bedroom flat, complete with full kitchen, dining, living, and media room. There was a fully stocked bar in its own room, and full-sized bathrooms off both bedrooms, one of which the Elvi took Cracker and caste him on the bed.\

